Record-update desugaring currently uses the FieldRegistry visible at
parse-discovery time, which only includes fields from
direct-import modules.  When the type's data decl lives in a
RE-EXPORTED module (e.g. UpdateSettings is re-exported from
Control.AutoUpdate but defined in Control.AutoUpdate.Types), the
re-exporter's lmFieldReg is empty and Types hasn't been loaded yet
(it's pulled in lazily at eval time when the body of
defaultUpdateSettings is forced).

Net result: warp's withDateCache raises
  record update: field(s) updateAction, updateThreadName not in registry
at runtime, killing the auto-update worker before sendResponse runs.

Fix path (deferred): defer record-update desugaring to eval time,
when the global module catalogue is complete.  See comments inside
the fixture for the load-amplification reasons every transitive-walk
attempt was rejected.

Remove _XFAIL once that refactor lands.
